{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And when the sun was going down.</b> At first it had not yet set, and likewise it is written לבוא [to come]." "<b>And dark. [עלטה]</b> Darkness, and its cognate [ריעו] is in Ezekiel. The meaning is that the night was cloudy, or its meaning is after the coming of the light seen in the clouds." "<b>And behold, a smoking furnace.</b> Like the form of a furnace from which smoke rises, and within it a torch of fire." "<b>Between the pieces.</b> Between the parts [הבתרים]. This is the oath, and likewise \"the calf which they cut in two\" (Jeremiah 34:18). Therefore after this it is written: On that day YHWH cut a covenant with Abram (Genesis 15:18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:44.492722423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}